WEBVTT

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:36.550
When I open my photo book, I see different sides of me. {purichou...}

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.320
Laughing, {warattari}

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.100
or playing it cool, in all the pictures. {sumashitari de...}

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.830
I don't wanna say, "what's with all these characters?" But... {nani kore...}

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.540
Isn't this too much fun? {arisugi...}

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.120
For real? {maji...}

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.330
I mean, thanks! {tte yuu ka...}

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.660
Even if I lose my way,  {maigo ni...}

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.270
my heart's egg {kokoro no...}

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.040
will be all right. Come back {daijoubu...}

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.730
to me! {modotteoide}

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.510
Hey, when we're together... {kimi to...}

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.230
Hop, step, jump!

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.840
Because you're here... {kimi ga...}

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.490
Drew, draw, drawn!

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.360
I'm always with you...  {kimi to...}

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.080
Chip, syrup, whip!

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.760
One more time,  {mou ichido...}

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.370
unlock my heart! {kokoro...}

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.140
I love you.  {daisuki yo}

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.600
All of you.  {minna}

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.490
I want to be next to you. {soba ni...}

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.800
Okay? {ne...}

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.950
Love ya! {suki yo}

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.250
Saya-sama, are we really going in there?

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.250
Let's give up on catching ghosts.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.810
What if there really are ghosts there?

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.400
That's exactly what I want!

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.030
This machine was created by concentrating the full power of the Yamabuki Concern.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.090
It's the Ghost Exterminating Vacuum Cleaner!

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.210
It sucks ghosts in through this opening,

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.950
thereby eliminating them!

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:17.990
And because it uses centrifugal force, no matter how many ghosts it sucks up, its power never diminishes!

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.020
And even better, if I catch a ghost...

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.700
You have such ghost-captivating beauty.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.260
I'm begging you, won't you become a Guardian?

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.790
No, be my bride!

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.950
It's pretty amazing that you can catch ghosts.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.150
I'll be waiting for you in middle school.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.770
Oh my, whatever shall I do?

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.420
No!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.420
Wait a minute, where are you all going?

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:53.470
I-It's a ghost! Switch, where's the switch?

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:11.820
Seriously!? Big Haunted House Adventure!

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:11.820
Episode 34

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.510
What?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:14.930
A haunted house?

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.310
Wow! I've always wanted to see a ghost!

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.710
I-Is that so? What an interesting tale.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.760
You're actually scared, aren't you?

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.650
Don't be absurd!

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.260
He's scared! He's scared!

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.470
So stupid.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.340
What's wrong, Amu?

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.100
W-Wrong? With what?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:37.880
You cannot tell by looking, but Amu-chan greatly dislikes the occult.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.860
You fool! Don't suddenly shout like that!

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.350
What's wrong, Hinamori-san?

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.240
Oh, nothing! It's nothing!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.290
Rima! You're awful!

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.110
King,

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.920
we should begin soon.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.610
Yes, you're right.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:01.890
Actually, many students have reported seeing ghosts at one of the houses nearby recently.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.770
They say they see something's shadow,

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.980
or hear strange noises.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.770
Not only that, some students have even become injured.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.910
It's the Guardians' responsibility to protect the students,

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.030
so we can't ignore this.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.560
Indeed.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.290
Well then, let's begin our investigation early tomorrow.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:28.040
Let us go, my subjects! Consider this additional special training toward my goal of world domination!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.190
I wonder if this is going to be okay.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.530
What should I do? I hate ghosts and stuff like that!

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.590
I have to think of something.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.160
I have a cold and a fever!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.240
Amu-chan.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.540
You're so obviously faking.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.020
Are you okay, Hinamori-san?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.920
If you have a fever, there's no need to push yourself.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.720
Oh, I'm fine.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.030
Sheesh.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.620
Ouch.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.780
Rima, are you okay?

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.870
Don't touch that!

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.470
Rima, look over there.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.440
That's not it!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.070
You don't understand!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.610
I have my own work to do as well.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.620
But you keep pushing everything off onto me!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.850
Hey, are you listening?

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:47.920
Dear!

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.850
Good grief.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.180
One, two, and...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.930
Bala-Balance!

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.870
Rima, let's do Bala-Balance, too!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.150
Bala-Balance!

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.020
Huh?

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.470
Amu-chan, get up.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:28.130
Today is the day we investigate the haunted house.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.390
I don't want to go.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:31.800
You're gonna skip, aren't you?

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.510
Leave this to me.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.920
Happy Angel!

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.660
She went back to sleep!

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.270
What'll I do?

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.540
I'm almost at the haunted house.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.390
You still feel like skipping, even after coming all this way?

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:53.740
Amu-chan, this is when the heroine shows her spirit!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.130
Fight! Fight!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.030
No matter what you say, scary stuff is still scary. I can't help it!

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:01.640
Man, El has it good.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.240
This is not good!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.010
A new Gwardian Character, Angel!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:09.540
I want to see ghosts, too.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:15.130
Okay, from now on I am God, and you'll play the part of the Love Love Angel!

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:18.200
The Love Love Angel?

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.750
I'm God! Where is an angel?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.990
Sir! Right here, Sir!

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:30.800
You must begin an investigation into the love triangle problems here in Heaven!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.640
Sir! Roger, Sir!

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.800
All right, it's not too late.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.340
I'll run away!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.570
Amu-chi!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.360
You can't escape now.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.400
This has the perfect atmosphere!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.870
It totally feels like ghosts will appear!

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:54.050
Ghosts are unscientific.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:58.930
There is a scientifically acceptable explanation for all strange phenomena.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:03.380
So what's the scientific explanation for our existence-dechu?

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.490
That is a point that causes him anguish every day.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.410
Won't you overlook it for now?

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:12.640
Let's hurry inside, Tadase!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:15.480
But Mashiro-san isn't here yet.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:18.570
If Rima doesn't come, is it cancelled?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.230
Hi, Rima-tan!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.080
Well then, shall we?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.050
Wait a minute!

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:27.810
We can't just go in there, can we?

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:31.510
We have to get permission from someone. Besides, it's probably locked.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.520
Oh, it opened.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.580
And there's no one here! It's finally getting serious!

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.700
All right, let's go!

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.020
N-No!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.470
It's pretty dirty.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.880
A house will quickly fall into disrepair when no one lives in it.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.610
Judging from its pitiful state, I'd say it's been empty for six months to a year.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.170
I think it would be worth cleaning.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.200
What's going on? It won't open!

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:11.460
That's common in homes that have become decrepit.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.930
The frame of the house shifts, causing the doors to not open.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:17.560
Generally, in these situations, if you just use enough force...

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.120
It looks like it's shifted quite a bit.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:22.940
That's no good!

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.430
Chairman, this also has a scientific explanation, right?

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:33.680
I-If there's a cavity under the foundation of the house,

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.910
the vibrations caused by a passing car or the like could...

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.300
Amu-chan, look!

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.070
Amu-chi!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:52.790
Let's go.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.200
I'm so excited!

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.030
Let's go, too.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:56.540
Yeah.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.180
Something was there!

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:01.790
Yeah.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:02.920
Let's go see!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:11.440
Doesn't this make your heart race, Amu-chi?

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:12.800
Yeah, it sure does.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:15.390
Another painting.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.810
Now that you mention it, there are paintings all over this house.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:23.480
It would appear that the owner of the house was an artist.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:25.750
Huh? Where's Mashiro-san?

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.990
Oh, Rima-tan runs pretty slow!

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.270
Rima, hurry, hurry!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.490
Oh dear, there's only one door!

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.440
Don't act so happy about it.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.810
If we leave, there'll be swarms of creepy dolls.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:01.730
That's right-dechu!

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:03.770
I can't hear you!

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.970
But this is troublesome.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.510
We hit a dead end quite quickly.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.280
Don't call me "prince!"

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.830
Bring a light!

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:17.700
Your King must be bathed in light!

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.270
W-Why?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:21.620
Nobody said "prince."

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.520
Fools! It was that "dead end!"

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.080
I see.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:30.140
"Fukurokouji" can sound like "fukuro ko ouji."

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:32.700
Note: "Fukurokouji" means "dead end" and "ouji" means "prince."

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:32.700
Why does that work?

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.820
It's your fault, so do something about it!

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:39.830
Spider.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.590
She ran away.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:48.960
By the way, I'd like to ask...

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.920
How do you make him undo his Character Change?

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:54.860
She's not here.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.870
Where could she have gone?

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.120
I thought this was it for sure.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.170
Ah! It's a Guardian Character!

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:10.660
Hey.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:14.840
You're the boy I met yesterday.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.730
The Queen's Chair, a Guardian?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.340
Why are you here?

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:22.870
Here.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:25.490
Oh!

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.500
It's important, isn't it?

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:30.320
Not especially.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.350
It's a picture of your family.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.830
It looks like you're close.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.360
What're you saying?

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.780
Are you stupid?

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.750
I never said I wanted to do this!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.670
I'm absolutely against ghost hunting!

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:49.620
Amu-chan, we found one!

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.460
I'm telling you, I've had enough of ghosts!

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:53.940
It's not a ghost.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.010
It's a Guardian Character.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.930
I don't care if it's a Guardian Character or...

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:57.560
What?

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:05.390
Is this...

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.670
A studio?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:09.970
Amu-chan.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:14.720
A Guardian Character?

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.570
But he's kind of transparent.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.770
Kuta-kun is on the verge of disappearing.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:20.660
What?

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:21.700
Why?

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:26.840
Kuta-kun is the Guardian Character of a boy named Shota, who lived here until six months ago.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.570
What happened to him?

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.640
He moved.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.260
I wanted to be an artist like my grandpa.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.610
He said

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.900
that my paintings were good.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.900
He told me they were well-drawn.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.590
That made me so happy.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.270
He wanted to be an artist.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.150
And Kuta was born from that desire.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:53.520
But...

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.510
He wants to be a painter?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:57.220
Let him.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:14:00.420
Painting all the time will be a hindrance to his studies.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.940
You're always so irresponsible!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:03.640
What did you say?

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.840
It's true!

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.300
If you were really thinking of what's best for him...

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:18.130
The only one who supported Shota's dream was his grandfather.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:20.900
But after he died,

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:24.380
his mother and father separated,

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.380
and he moved away from this house.

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:28.440
And so...

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:31.270
Shota-kun's dream faded away.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.820
Oh no.

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:36.140
If he forgets his dream, his Guardian Character will vanish.

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:39.780
I still haven't been able to get Shota-kun to notice me.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:42.700
And to just fade away...

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.430
If I have this, it just reminds me of the past.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:50.250
But these are the paints that my grandpa gave me; I can't just throw them away.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.540
So I thought I'd bring them back here.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:57.880
I wonder why was I so happy when I lived here.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:01.350
Kuta?

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:02.950
Kuta!

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:06.210
Back then,

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.390
I felt like I could be anything I wanted.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.300
But now,

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:11.370
I don't want to paint.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:13.880
Kuta!

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.530
That sound!

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.440
Let's go!

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:21.670
Rima.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.830
I sense a bad presence.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:26.800
What should we do? What should we do?

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.100
A Guardian Egg!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.380
Maybe it's...

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.790
I don't want it.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.080
I don't want any of it.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:36.440
Amu-chan, that kid!

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.710
Yeah, that's definitely Shota-kun.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:42.640
But he looks a little odd.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:43.850
Hinamori-san!

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.410
Who's the kid?

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:49.670
It would appear that something bad is happening.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:50.120
Yeah.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:53.470
You went to the trouble of bringing this to me, but...

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:57.150
I don't want pictures like this one anymore.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:04.530
There's an X on Kuta's egg!

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:05.860
Rima.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.050
Character Transform!

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:07.760
Okay.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.430
My heart:

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:13.330
Unlock!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:54.370
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:56.280
My heart:

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.670
Unlock!

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:15.270
Character Transformation: Clown Drop!

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.110
White!

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:22.500
Grey!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.630
Black!

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.430
It turned into an X Character!

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:28.070
So that's an X Character.

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:30.460
Dark Canvas!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.520
What's that? He's imitating my special move!

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:37.990
Amu-chan, it's our turn!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:38.440
Right.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.750
Colorful Canvas!

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:43.800
Dark Canvas!

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:48.720
No way.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.720
Colorful Canvas isn't working!

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:55.100
Dark Canvas!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.890
Musashi, Character Change!

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:58.330
Very well.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.570
Chairman, you're so cool!

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:06.400
Naturally.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:07.780
Black!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:09.280
Black!

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.990
Black!

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.550
Things won't go back to the way they were.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.820
I was so happy then.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:22.210
Grandpa was here, Mom and Dad could laugh.

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:25.920
But things will never

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:28.180
go back to the way they were!

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:40.770
Rima.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:42.840
Are you stupid?

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.040
Of course things won't be the same.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.410
How could they,

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.900
when you've thrown away your dream?

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.790
Shut up!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:53.780
Be quiet! Be quiet!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.910
We won't be quiet.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.610
Rima's exactly right.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:01.290
No matter how sad you feel, you can't forget who you want to be!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.490
You should always hold on to your dreams!

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.700
Learn to smile on your own!

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:09.170
Let's go, Miki!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:09.800
Yeah!

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.090
Negative Heart:

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.340
Lock On!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.400
Open Heart!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:41.180
Shota-kun really loves painting.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.340
His dream will definitely come true.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.960
He'll become an artist one day.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:47.690
Thank you.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:49.020
Sure.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:20:00.030
I don't really get why, but it looks like everything's okay.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:03.420
I'll expect a full report later.

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:04.890
Fine.

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.540
Don't worry.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.380
Leave the repairs to me.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.570
Put things back the way they were!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:21.250
Let's gently fix everything!

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:24.710
Remake Honey!

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:32.320
Huh?

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.950
What am I doing?

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:41.180
Why is this in such good shape now?

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.460
Grandpa's sketchbook.

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:49.100
It was so dirty that I couldn't see anything.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.570
What's this?

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:56.550
Your grandpa could see Guardian Characters.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.240
Here.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.630
It's important.

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:02.700
That picture...

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:07.000
I-It's not especially important.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.670
Aren't you stubborn.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.540
Shut up.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:11.710
Say...

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.110
It'll be good

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.250
when you're able to see him.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.270
Huh?

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:25.290
I was really scared,

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:28.200
but it turns out that there weren't any ghosts.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.550
It was just a Guardian Character that was about to vanish, who wanted someone to notice him,

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:34.260
and that turned into ghost problems.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.710
Good grief. He certainly caused trouble.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:39.570
It must've been tough to not have any strength;

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:42.100
to only be able to move small things.

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.090
What? Only small things?

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.200
Then what was that...

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.640
What could it have been?

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:56.300
He said it was all he could do to move that little doll.

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:57.440
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:59.990
S-So you're saying...

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:04.230
Man, give me a break!

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:07.060
Let's go home, too.

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:07.770
Yeah!

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:41.130
You can't think that there's {kotaenante...}

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:44.510
an answer out there somewhere, you see. {arutte...}

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:50.810
Because the only place you'll find it is inside you. {kotaenante...}

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:53.050
Ain't that cool? {kakkoii...}

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:58.000
The fact is, all you're truly feeling... {arinomama...}

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:00.330
Yup, it's love! {yappa...}

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:05.890
And right now, all those feelings are welling up. {ima no mama...}

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:09.660
So head toward the sun, give it everything you've got. {sei ippai...}

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:13.270
Try bustin' through. {butsukete...}

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.640
Face forward, raise your head up high. {maemuite...}

00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:20.550
There's no time to cry. {naiteru...}

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:23.800
A passionate kiss! This "youthful" kiss! {jounetsu...}

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:27.800
I love you when you're trying your best, like now.  {ima ganbatteru...}

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:31.050
The best kiss! This "all-out" kiss! {saiko no...}

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:35.030
I want to show you these feelings that fill my heart. {mune ippai...}

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:39.730
I L-O-V-E Y-O-U.

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:49.990
I am number one today!

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:54.040
It's finally happening!

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.040
The wedding!

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:56.710
Huh? Whose? Who's getting married?

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:57.250
It couldn't be...

00:23:57.250 --> 00:23:59.380
Amu-chan's dad?

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:01.620
My dad's already married!

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:04.430
The guy getting married is Amu-chan's crush!

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:05.790
Her first love.

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:06.990
My first love?

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:09.770
He's getting married?!

00:24:09.770 --> 00:24:11.020
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:12.560
My First Love's Wedding Cake!

00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:14.940
Oh, it's so romantic!

00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:16.480
Nope, it might be really stormy.

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:20.020
First loves never work out.
